=== phase 4: shuffled-donor control (is the content row-specific?)
==============================================================================
  Each row receives the head outputs ANOTHER row's DONOR QUESTION produced, and is scored against its own donor gold (`own`) and against the donor row's (`donor`). Every artefactual way phase 3 could succeed -- a mask not really restricted to k heads, a perturbation knocking the residual off-distribution, a scorer counting the wrong thing -- is indifferent to WHICH row supplied the values. Real transfer is not: `own` must collapse and `donor` must rise.
       top-8 shuffled:  own= 87.3% donor= 57.1% kept=  0.4%   (unshuffled first was 87.3%)
     ALL 224 shuffled:  own= 76.2% donor= 68.7% kept=  0.0%   (unshuffled first was 90.5%)

  !! the answer did NOT follow the donor -- `own` stayed at 87.3% while receiving another row's values. Phase 3's curve is an artefact of perturbing this site, not transfer.

